  "@id": "https://w3id.org/pices/odis/records/zenodo-23569266.jsonld",
  "@type": "Dataset",
  "name": "Japanese Ocean Flux Data Sets with Use of Remote Sensing Observations (J-OFURO)",
  "description": "Japanese Ocean Flux data sets with Use of Remote sensing Observations (J-OFURO). Ocean surface flux data sets were constructed mainly using satellite data and are as follows: SWR: Shortwave Radiation (monthly) LWR: Longwave Radiation (monthly) LHF: Latent Heat Flux (monthly, 3days) SHF: Sensible Heat Flux (monthly) MF_E: Momentum Flux from ERS (monthly,10days) MF_Q: Momentum Flux form QSCAT (monthly, Daily) AIRT: Air Temperatre (monthly) ALTI: Altimeter Product (cycle) You can use the J-OFURO data freely for scientific use. If J-OFURO used in your publication or document, users are requested to reference the source of the data such as \"J-OFURO data used in this study have been obtained from J-OFURO web site (http://dtsv.scc.u-tokai.ac.jp/j-ofuro/) and Kubota et al.,2002 (see following). Also we would appreciate your sending a reprint or copy of your publication or document to our address. Kubota, M., N. Iwasaka, S. Kizu, M. Konda, and K. Kutsuwada, (2002): Japanese ocean flux data sets with use of remote sensing observations (J-OFURO). J Oceanogr, 58, 213-225.\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: To derive homogenous data with high resolution using analysis and satellite data for obtaining globally-covered fluxes between ocean and atmosphere.",
  "url": "https://zenodo.org/records/23569267",
